{"id":5378,"date":"2025-11-10T10:30:00","date_gmt":"2025-11-10T09:30:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.jouwweb.nl\/blog\/?p=5378"},"modified":"2025-11-06T14:12:59","modified_gmt":"2025-11-06T13:12:59","slug":"optimize-images-rank-higher-in-google","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/optimize-images-rank-higher-in-google\/","title":{"rendered":"Optimize Images: Rank Higher in Google"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A key part of ranking higher in Google is optimizing your website&#8217;s images. Many businesses focus on text, but images also offer opportunities to rank higher in search results. Especially if you offer a visual product or service, your images are important not only for your appearance but also for your SEO!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In this blog we give you 3 tips that you can easily apply yourself.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1: Choose the correct file type<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Your website&#8217;s loading speed is a key factor for search engines. To make your website faster, it&#8217;s important to have the right image file type. Uploading your images in the correct file type ensures your website loads faster.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To give you a good overview, we&#8217;ve listed the three most commonly used file types. This way, you can see which file types are best for your images:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>File types<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>JPEG<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>PNG<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Transparent background<\/td><td>No<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>File size<\/td><td>Small<\/td><td>Large<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Recommended for<\/td><td>Photography, large images, colorful images<\/td><td>Logos, screenshots, graphs, images with text<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All images you upload to Webador are automatically converted to WebP format by our system, guaranteeing the best loading times.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2: Add ALT text<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The second tip is to add alternative text to your images, also called &#8220;alt text.&#8221; Alt text is often added for visually impaired users, but it also helps search engines better understand your images. Google can&#8217;t &#8220;see&#8221; your image; it only reads the alt text. So if you don&#8217;t have that text, Google won&#8217;t understand what your image is about.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Adding ALT text to your website is super easy, just follow these steps:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Go to the image for which you want to set alt text and click on the image:<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Click on the gear:<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"425\" src=\"https:\/\/www.jouwweb.nl\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-135953-1024x425.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5379\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-135953-1024x425.png 1024w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-135953-300x125.png 300w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-135953-768x319.png 768w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-135953.png 1534w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">3. A pop-up window will appear with &#8220;Alternative Text.&#8221; Enter your text here. Briefly describe what your image is about:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"430\" src=\"https:\/\/www.jouwweb.nl\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-140119-1024x430.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5380\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-140119-1024x430.png 1024w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-140119-300x126.png 300w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-140119-768x322.png 768w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-06-140119.png 1525w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3: Change your file name<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The third tip for optimizing your images is to change your file name.<br>Chances are, the image you want to upload to your website has an unusual file name. A valuable tip to make your images easier to find is to change the file name before uploading them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These are the 3 most important tips for optimizing your images. By choosing the right file type, adding ALT text, and adjusting the file name, you&#8217;ll ensure your images rank higher in search engines.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-light-gray-background-color has-background\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-not-stacked-on-mobile is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n